bound-lock/1 about="All Head source lines under the existing 0.1.5 ceiling. No local identity fingerprint or duplicated call-resolution wrapper is delivered; contracts remain in the lock and source comments are concise." at=policy:head/verified-delivery/0.1.6 by=target form=interval measure=source-lines role=writes scope=source/lines value=0..2600
bound-lock/1 about="Allow one offer that is not of class read, up to a number of times." at=policy:head/surface by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=prompt/can value=source|operation|times
bound-lock/1 about="An API already says what it offers, where it is reached and how access to it is proven. head reads that document once, compiles it into lines its place pins by digest, and from then on answers by those lines: which operation reads, what it asks, what it answered. It names no kind of source and no client: what it reads is said by the worlds it adopts, and what it asks through is what the client declares. [Connect any API](docs/connect-any-api.md) shows each level of access.\n\nA person does three things. **Found a place**: a folder whose lock is the place, its root key kept in the keychain; the first source connected with no place founds `~/place` on the same yes. **Connect a source**: hand head an API document, and an overlay beside it when it says too little; it is compiled once, pinned, and every offer is listed with its class. **Ask**: read an operation. head obtains access the first time, as the document declares it, calls only what reads, types the answer and lands a receipt.\n\nAccess comes at three levels, and the place says which. **None**: the document states that a read needs nothing, or says nothing about access at all; then head tries the read once with nothing attached, and keeps what it saw as a receipt. **A declared flow**: the document, or its overlay, declares how access is obtained, as an Arazzo profile: a form, a one-time code, a choice, a provider's page. head runs it once per issuer and keeps only the token, in the keychain. **A secret entered by hand**: a key or a password, only where the place's root allows it, entered on head's own one-time page and never through the model.\n\nWhat head never does. It never guesses how access is proven: when a document does not state it, only a read is tried, with nothing attached, and nothing else is called. It never calls an operation that is not a read without the person's yes, nor past what the place allows; a place that would stand on another's lock as its parent is refused by name, since composing two places' policies is bound's. It never lets a secret reach the model, a file, an answer or an argument. And it never raises a ceiling to make room: what outgrows one is split by responsibility." at=policy:head/docs/0.1.4 by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/idea value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="An MCP server that reads any API by its document: access asked once per issuer, every answer typed by the world that compiled it, every read kept with a signed receipt." at=policy:head/docs by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/what value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="An earlier call of {operation} on {source} landed its intent {intent} and no receipt: look at what it would have changed with closes={intent}, then act again." at=policy:head/surface by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/open value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="An intent an earlier act left open, by the scope it was named under: once this read lands, it closes that intent with the read-s digest. Look at what the act would have changed." at=policy:head/surface by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=tool/look/closes value=string
bound-lock/1 about="An intent an earlier act left open, by the scope it was named under: once this read lands, it closes that intent with the read-s digest. Look at what the act would have changed." at=policy:head/verbs/0.1.4 by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=tool/ask/closes value=string
bound-lock/1 about="An overlay for the document, the same way; optional." at=policy:head/surface by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=tool/connect/overlay value=string
bound-lock/1 about="Answer latency depends on reuse of valid readings and an in-process Bound host; the declared answer ceiling remains unchanged." at=policy:head/release-checks/0.1.4 by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=answer/seconds/rests-on value=bound/read-reuse|bound/in-process-host
bound-lock/1 about="Answer the person in their words. Never show them a coordinate, a digest, a pin or a ledger epoch a cell carries — those are for you to act on — unless they ask why, or share a place, whose digest is what they send. Use claim only with the person-s exact words, never with a conclusion of yours." at=policy:head/claims/0.1.5 by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/instructions value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Answered from the receipt {scope} ({digest}), as the source answered it at {at}, within the reuse the place allows: nothing was called; nothing typed was kept of it, so the fold typed it again." at=policy:head/surface by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/reread value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Answered from what was kept for {scope} ({digest}), as the source answered it at {at}, within the reuse the place allows: nothing was called and nothing folded." at=policy:head/surface by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/reused value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Any API, read by its document" at=policy:head/docs by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=docs/tagline value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Ask head, and nothing changes but the receipts of what was read. With nothing: what this device has connected. A source: its region, what it offers; with an operation and its parameters, one read of an offer of class read, answered with the receipt the device key landed for it, or, while the place allows reuse, the answer kept for it and nothing called. A view: as bound folds it. card: what is open, and the card do needs. lines: a lot for the person to sign. Nothing that is not a read is ever called. An answer about one place ends with its card, valid from it." at=policy:head/marks/0.1.5 by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=tool/ask value=place|source|operation|args|view|card|key|lines|why|history|closes|sources
bound-lock/1 about="Ask me before {operation} on {source} is called, every time. Plan this line for me to sign:" at=policy:head/surface by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=prompt/ask/text value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Ask the person before an offer is called, every time." at=policy:head/surface by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=prompt/ask value=source|operation
bound-lock/1 about="Asked of a link, the transport it is read by: the lines of head-s profile the place was born with, and who laid them." at=policy:head/verbs/0.1.6 by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=tool/connect/why value=boolean
bound-lock/1 about="Call one offer that is not of class read, only as far as the person allowed it and after their yes when they asked to be asked. The intent lands before the call and the receipt after; a call that never answered stays open until a look closes it." at=policy:head/surface by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=tool/act value=place|source|operation|args
bound-lock/1 about="Clone, `npm ci && npm test`. A vector that gives you a different answer is the contribution: send it with what it printed. Lines land through the fold, never by hand; when a page and the lock disagree, the lock is right." at=policy:head/docs by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/contributing value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Closed {intent} by this read ({digest}). It counts as done: act runs again only within what is still allowed." at=policy:head/surface by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/closed value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Connect a source to a place from its document." at=policy:head/surface by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=prompt/connect value=place|source|document
bound-lock/1 about="Connect a source to a place, once the person says yes: its document, and an overlay beside it, laid whatever its kind and compiled once by whichever world reads it — or open, with the line that pays it — into what the source offers and how access is proven, pinned by digest. Nothing is called. A document at an address may be read as a source the place connected, with the access it holds, and checked against its digest. A package another place shared is connected whole: its lock as the document, named by its digest. A site alone or a folder is looked for its document first, before anything is founded. With no place yet, the first connect founds the person-s place on one yes that also lets head read the source." at=policy:head/connect/0.1.4 by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=tool/connect value=place|source|document|overlay|digest|via|accept|operation|args
bound-lock/1 about="Connect any API" at=policy:head/docs by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/page/connect-any-api/heading value=lock
