bound-lock/1 about="{operation} on {source} is allowed {allowed} times and was done {done}: nothing was called. A wider allowance the person signs pays it, as far as the place-s own cap allows." at=policy:head/surface/0.1.1g by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/not-allowed value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{origin} is already in use from {dir}: ask what it offers with look, or connect another document to that place with connect." at=policy:head/surface/0.1.1g by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/use-held value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{origin} is in use from {dir}, as {source}: read-only, every call that is not a read capped at zero, reads granted until {until}. What it offers, and how access is proven:" at=policy:head/surface/0.1.1g by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/used value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{origin} is not encrypted and is not this device: nothing was sent to it. Its encrypted address pays it." at=policy:head/surface/0.1.1g by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/insecure-origin value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{origin} published no document a world compiles: tried {tried}. The place stays founded; a document named by the person is connected to it with connect." at=policy:head/surface/0.1.1g by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/use-none value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{place} admits a key named {name} already, or this key under another name: nothing was admitted. Another name pays it, or the old admission withdrawn by the place-s root." at=policy:head/surface/0.1.1g by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/key-taken value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{place} admits no content transport, so no link is inspected there. These lines admit one, for you to sign: {lines}" at=policy:head/link/0.1.5 by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/transport-missing value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{place} admits no field for who carried a statement here, its witness, so nothing was kept. Whoever configures {place} can sign these lines: {lines}" at=policy:head/claims/0.1.5 by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/claims-unadmitted value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{place} covers {coverage} for the key that would sign; {scope} is not in it, so nothing was asked, called or signed. Whoever configures {place} can sign these lines:" at=policy:head/surface by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/not-covered value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{place} does not allow retained reads of {source} to be inspected. Whoever configures it can sign this line:" at=policy:head/surface by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/history-undeclared value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{place} has no source connected: there is nothing to pack. Nothing was written." at=policy:head/surface/0.1.1 by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/share-none value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{place} moved since the card {card} was asked, or none was: nothing was done. Ask for its card again, and act on what it shows." at=policy:head/verbs/0.1.4 by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/card-stale value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{place} reads a #bound: link by the transport head-s profile laid at its birth: these lines are head-s, never yours, and none of them grants anything of yours. A transport that carries something of yours is asked for the first time it is needed." at=policy:head/surface/0.1.6 by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/why-transport value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{place} was acted in, and its receipts did not close: {why}" at=policy:head/surface/0.1.2 by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/receipts-open value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{place} was born before its wire named who witnesses a widening, so nothing its root signs as one lands there until it does. head proposes this lot — the wire it stands on withdrawn and said again with the witness, signed by the root alone: plan it, then land it; nothing is migrated:" at=policy:head/surface by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/unwitnessed value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{place} would stand on {parent} as its parent lock. Composing a parent-s policy with a child-s is bound-s to do, and this head does not: nothing was adopted, called or signed. A package another place shared is connected by the digest its sender sent apart from it." at=policy:head/surface/0.1.1 by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/parent-lock value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{sources} backed that {field} is {value} ({marks}). I don-t know whether they are independent." at=policy:head/surface/0.1.6-backed by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/agreed-unknown value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{sources} backed that {field} is {value} ({marks}). Nobody has declared that they share lineage." at=policy:head/surface/0.1.6-backed by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/agreed-undeclared value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{sources} backed that {field} is {value} ({marks}): {source} looks like the same lineage as {other} and may add nothing." at=policy:head/surface/0.1.6-backed by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/agreed-lineage value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{source} answered {operation} at {at}: the answer this conversation already holds ({digest}), kept by the receipt {receipt}. Nothing was called and nothing is sent again." at=policy:head/kept/0.1.5 by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/kept value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{source} answered {operation} from {origin} at {at}: backed by the key {by} at epoch {epoch}, receipt {digest}. It rests on the pin {pin} of {source}, landed at epoch {pinned}, and on the world {worlds}. Who crossed it is not said: bound computes no encounters yet." at=policy:head/surface/0.1.6-backed by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/why value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{source} answered {status} to {operation} at {at}, and no world typed the answer here {why}: head hands no body." at=policy:head/numbers/0.1.5 by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/untyped value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{source} answered {status} to {operation} at {at}. What its document declares of the answer, one value a line:" at=policy:head/numbers/0.1.5 by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/answered value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{source} answered {status} to {operation} at {at}: nothing, as it holds it today at this resolution, not that there never is. Its receipt stands; there is no body to hand." at=policy:head/surface/0.1.6-answered by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/answered-nothing value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{source} backed that {field} is {value}, at {at}." at=policy:head/surface/0.1.6-backed by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/forked value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{source} backed that {field} is {value}, at {at}; no other requested source backed this field. This is incomplete evidence, not disagreement." at=policy:head/surface/0.1.6-backed by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/partial value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{source} compiled here as {got}, not as the {pin} the package names: the same documents compile otherwise under this head. The place holds what it compiled, and the package is refused. A package shared from a head at this release pays it." at=policy:head/surface/0.1.1g by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/package-pin value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{source} declares no origin: nothing was called. The person-s line allow/origin/{source}, naming where it is reached, pays it." at=policy:head/surface/0.1.1g by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/no-origin value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{source} declares several origins ({origins}): the person picks one as region/{source} origin; none is a default, production least of all. Nothing was called." at=policy:head/surface by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/pick-origin value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{source} did not grant access the way it declares: nothing was kept and nothing was called. Entering it again, as {source} accepts it, pays it." at=policy:head/surface/0.1.1g by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/login-refused value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{source} does not state how access to {operation} is proven, and only a read is ever tried with nothing attached: nothing was called. An overlay beside its document that states the access of {method} {path} pays it." at=policy:head/connect/0.1.4 by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/access-unstated value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{source} is a document of a profile the world does not read: {why}. It was laid and taken back; nothing was connected. A document of a profile a world reads pays it." at=policy:head/surface/0.1.1g by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/document-unsupported value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{source} is a document the world could not parse: {why}. It was laid and taken back; nothing was connected. The document mended where {why} points pays it." at=policy:head/surface/0.1.1g by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/document-unparsed value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{source} is connected to {place}, and head may read it: ask {operation} again, with {args}." at=policy:head/birth/0.1.4 by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/ready value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{source} is connected to {place}: {offers} offers, {reads} of them read; each callable by its name or in the person-s words, none listed until used. Pinned as {pin}. How access is proven, and where it is reached:" at=policy:head/surface/0.1.6 by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/connected value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{source} is pinned otherwise than when {operation} was read at {at}, so what was kept of it stands no longer: it was read again." at=policy:head/kept/0.1.5 by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/kept-changed value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{source} is reached through a provider that needs a client the person registered: sign keys/access/{source}/<scheme> client with it. head invents none. Nothing was called." at=policy:head/surface by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/no-client value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{source} names two different documents ({why}), and a source is one: neither was read. It was laid and taken back; nothing was connected. One document for {source} pays it." at=policy:head/surface/0.1.1g by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/document-collision value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{source} offers no {operation}: nothing was called. What it offers is listed by look at 1." at=policy:head/surface/0.1.1g by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/unknown-operation value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{source} offers {more} more, listed only once used: each is callable by its name or in the person-s words." at=policy:head/surface/0.1.6 by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/more-offers value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{source} proves access to {operation} by {kinds}, and none of them says how its token rides a request: nothing was called. An overlay that says it pays it." at=policy:head/surface/0.1.1g by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/no-adapter value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{source} referred to {by} before it was here: compiled again, its pin now {pin}. Nothing was reconnected and nothing was called." at=policy:head/surface by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/resolved value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{source} refers to {refs}, which no document of this place declares yet: a demand, paid when the document that declares it is connected — {source} is then compiled again, never reconnected." at=policy:head/surface by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/unresolved value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{source} refused the read without access and named who issues it: {issuer}. head observed how — its metadata, the steps, a client where the server registers one — and the next read signs in there, on head-s page, once; its token and refresh are kept in this keychain and renewed on use." at=policy:head/surface/0.1.1g by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/authorizer-observed value=lock
